<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !Objects.isNull(c) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !Objects.isNull(c) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[(int)i]);</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the collection `c` is not null, then for every valid index `i` in the list, the element at index `i` in the list is equal to the element at index `i` in the collection `c`. Note that `c.toArray()` is used to convert the collection to an array to facilitate element comparison by index.
--------------------
